  "facts": [
    "The Joseph‑Samson Bridge–Tunnel, built in the 1980s by Quebec’s Ministry of Transportation, carries six lanes of traffic, a bike lane, and sidewalks across the Saint‑Charles River before plunging underground.",
    "After crossing the river, the tunnel passes beneath Gare du Palais train station and the SAAQ headquarters, known locally as the Jean Lesage Building, showcasing a rare blend of over‑and‑under infrastructure.",
    "Named after former mayor Joseph‑Octave Samson, the structure features a reversible lane system—two lanes above and one below—allowing traffic flow to adapt to peak‑hour demands."
